**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The app scope composes the item-model store over its library database for S6 item-copy resolution and the S7 Items panel (.spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it composes the SQLite library proxies over the configured locations; 001 §O 'Add item from library model…'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `AppContext` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`, documented in one line (the item-model store over the app's library database, spec 0050 S7.1), set by `compose` (step 89) to `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 211) beside the other database stores, so `create` and `recreateLibrary` carry it. No window reads it in this section, and no other field changes. (2) Tests: `AppContextTests` gains `the app scope serves the Built-in item models from its library database`: `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "AppContextTests")`'s `itemModels.listItemModels ()` answers exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` ordered by name, because the start-up import (steps 95, 100) brought the shipped item models into its database.

**Acceptance.** After the composition, `AppContext.itemModels` MUST be the database item-model store of the app scope's library and serve the Built-in item models; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app scope serves the Built-in item models from its library database`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
